    "creatorEnglish": "Cairo Congress Tuning Committee",
    "creatorArabic": "لجنة التنغيم في مؤتمر القاهرة",
    "commentsEnglish": "\"This committee was put together before the congress to undertake these measurements in preparation for the congress and consisted of the members: Muṣtafā Riḍā, Najīb Naḥḥās, Ṣafar 'Ali, Muḥammad al-'Aqqād, Aḥmad Amīn al-Dīk, Muṣtafā al-'Aqqād, Kantonā, Muḥammad 'Abd al-Wahāb, Darwīsh al-Ḥarīrī, Kostakī, Armanāk, Muḥammad Fatḥī, Ya'qūb 'Abd al-Wahāb and Maḥmūd Zakī. These measurements were obtained by asking Muṣtafā Riḍā and Muḥammad al-'Aqād to separately tune their qanūns to a tuning fork resonating at the frequency of the note \"rāst\". The committee then measured both of their qanūns with a sonometer and only found a differencof 1/10 cm (1 mm) only between the notes dūgāh, nawā and ḥusaynī\" Shawqi (1969:48).\n\nThe tuning system in this table has been moved down from the note rāst to yegāh, making the difference between the two qanūns on the pitch classes 'ushayrān, rāst and dūgāh.\n\nNeither Shawqī nor the original Congress text mention if the 1mm difference was higher or lower in pitch. By analysing the string length measurements and comparing them to the pitch classes produced by using ratios, the difference is indeed negligible. For reference, on a string of 1000 mm, 1 mm equals 0.173 cents.\n\n'ushayrān - 9/8 - 8888.9 mm\nrāst - 4/3 - 750 mm\ndūgāh - 3/2 - 6666.6 mm\n\nShawqi (1969:52) further comments that according to Badrān (1957:157) the measurements that the committee of the 1932 Congress documented amounted to a difference of 18/100 of a centimeter (1 4/5 of a mm) for the notes segāh and awj, and between 6/100 and 9/100 of a centimeter for all the other notes except rāst and kurdān - the octave of rāst. Though again whether the differences were higher or lower is not mentioned.\n\nBadrān, Muḥammad Tawfīq Muṣtafa (1957)\nhttps://search.worldcat.org/search?q=ti=H%CC%A3alqah%20...%20li-Bah%CC%A3th%20al-Mu%CC%84si%CC%84qa%CC%81%20al-%CA%BBArabi%CC%84yah",
    "commentsArabic": "",
