    "creatorArabic": "الخلعي وراغب",
    "commentsEnglish": "Also in Shawqi, Youssef. Qiyās al-Sullam al-Mūsīqī al-'Arabī. Dar al-Kutub, Cairo, 1969. pp. 28-29.\n\nShawqi says that whole tone (888 mm) doesn't add up to 10:9 or 9:8 as one would expect (1969:29) but the descrepency is only -1.732 cents and is infact the same as the descrepency between the perfect fourth (750 mm / 4:3) and the perfect fifth (666 mm / 3:2) which he states are correct in al-Khulaʿī's measurements.",
