    "creatorEnglish": "Meshshāqa",
    "creatorArabic": "مشّاقة، ميخائيل",
    "commentsEnglish": "The tuning system is printed in the book as \"String Length\" but it is actually listed as Fret Divisions i.e. the list is ascending as:\n\nYegāh = 000\n102\n201\n298\n392\n483\n572\n658\n742\n823\n903\n980\n1054\n1127\n1197\n1266\n1332\n1397\n1460\n1521\n1580\n1638\n1693\n1748\n1800 = nawā\n\nTherefore as nawā is the octave, we deduce that the string length is 3600 and we must recalculate the tuning systems pitch classes as 3600-102, 3600-201 etc...",
    "commentsArabic": "",
