  {
    "id": "alsabbagh_1954",
    "titleEnglish": "Contemporary Arabic Tuning 24-Tone",
    "titleArabic": "السلم العربي الحالي 24 نغمة",
    "year": "1954",
    "sourceEnglish": "Unknown Source",
    "sourceArabic": "مصدر غير معروف",
    "sourcePageReferences": [
      {
        "sourceId": "alsabbagh_1954",
        "page": "47"
      }
    ],
    "creatorEnglish": "al-Ṣabbāgh",
    "creatorArabic": "الصبّاغ، توفيق",
    "commentsEnglish": "In Ṣabbāgh's previous book (1950:173) he gives The Contemporary Arabic tuning system as one of 19 tones. In his follow up book (1954:47) he states the following:\n\n\"It appears from the preceding pitch tables that our primary and secondary tones consist of nineteen degrees, and it has been stated in al-Dalīl al-Mūsīqī al-ʿĀmm (The General Musical Guide) that these are, by default, considered the current Arabic scale.\n\nAfter that, I observed a tendency among many to preserve the names of the well-known twenty-four quarter-tones familiar to us. So I proceeded to add seven additional degrees, thereby allowing our scale to encompass the conventional theoretical tones as well. In this way, we have preserved the names of the twenty-four quarters used in our tradition, leaving no room for objection by anyone.\n\nThus, our current Arabic scale becomes composed of twenty-five degrees, among which are twenty-four unequal intervals, as defined in the following table.\"\n\nṢabbāgh then proceeds to give the 24-tone tuning system in fret divisions as fractions ratios, vibrating string length, number of commas between each pitch class and the note names for each pitch class starting from rāst.\n\nThe tuning values inputted here are inversions of Ṣabbāgh's fret divisions fraction ratios into string length fraction ratios, for example: 1/9 becomes 9/8 but we provide the originals here for reference:\n\n0, 13/256, 1/16, 17/201, 1/9, 5/32, 1/6, 19/102, 1/5, 17/81, 1/4, 31/112, 13/45, 217/729, 1/3, 47/128, 71/189, 235/603, 11/27, 7/16, 393/883, 549/1200, 7/15, 115/243, 1/2\n\n10000, 9492, 9375, 9155, 8889, 8438, 8333, 8137, 8000, 7901, 7500, 7233, 7111, 7023, 6667, 6328, 6243, 6103, 5926, 5625, 5549, 5425, 5333, 5267, 5000",
    "commentsArabic": "",
    "tuningSystemPitchClasses": [
