    "creatorEnglish": "Allami",
    "creatorArabic": "اللامي",
    "commentsEnglish": "Created by using al-Ṣabbāgh's (1954) 24-tone tuning system which is based on the syntonic comma (81/80). al-Ṣabbāgh's note names match al-Shawwā's 24-note name system which makes them compatible and allows for the inclusion of al-Shawwā's additional note names (1946:13) by using al-Shawwā's one comma higher or one comma lower delineation for each of these additional note names. Although Shawwā provides 5 extra note names only four are needed because one of them, nahāwand, is given as lower than kūrdī by one comma (6/5 x 80/81), equalling the ratio 32/27, which is already assigned to nīm kurdī/nahāwand in al-Ṣabbāgh's system.\n\n- Khyam Allami",
